Doing a quick check on tooled horns, monster MR, and Croesus, he'd 
have a base 4/9 chance of resisting the horn and 10/23 chance of 
resisting a /oSleep ray that hits (4/5 chance of a hit, assuming 
Croesus isn't wearing armor); the equation is:

    MR/(100+AL-DL)

where MR is the monster's magic resistance (40, for Croesus), AL is 
the attack level of the incoming effect (10 for tools, like the horn, 
12 for a wand), and DL is the lower of the monster's level or 50 
(base 20 for Croesus, not counting !oGL and drained levels). Stormy's 
likely drained a few of those, but the odds'll likely be in the same 
ballpark.
